{"id": "EUVD-2026-80469", "enisaUuid": "814f9690-9862-3617-a011-d18f1c39de96", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nmedia: qcom: iris: use disable_irq() during power-off\n\nThe IRQ is registered as a threaded IRQ.\n\nUsing disable_irq_nosync() in iris_vpu_power_off() does not wait\nfor an already queued threaded IRQ handler to complete before\nreturning.\n\nAs a result, a threaded IRQ handler may still run after the VPU has\nbeen powered down and access hardware registers after power-off.\n\nReplace disable_irq_nosync() with disable_irq() so the power-off path\nwaits for any in-flight threaded IRQ handler to complete before\nreturning.", "datePublished": "2026-09-16T10:31:38", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T08:54:02", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/ff98cd2b8b54cf96bccace2f7b7e4775cdccaf02", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/d7f34cbaced92069400fc5d71fefe3cb4c748da8", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/b9c2215bdedc9c532a7e9d57ec49ee1b6381f863"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-89869", "GHSA-5mhw-wrx9-mqjj"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.21, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "291ef71f-dff6-3155-beeb-a38d06f0b9c1", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "bb8a95aa038e099f5ec82c466e996b006e05abd7 <b9c2215bdedc9c532a7e9d57ec49ee1b6381f863"}, {"id": "40748ce6-bcdd-352d-94fb-1ed2acbdb5b7", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "40accf2a-396d-3d00-b916-22377d9c39d2", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "423e5c24-d0fa-387f-bab3-c4970411def0", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.15"}, {"id": "85ad89e9-12d7-3582-9603-836fab26bd72", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "bb8a95aa038e099f5ec82c466e996b006e05abd7 <ff98cd2b8b54cf96bccace2f7b7e4775cdccaf02"}, {"id": "987f19de-552b-3778-92b7-2ba1daeee896", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "bb8a95aa038e099f5ec82c466e996b006e05abd7 <d7f34cbaced92069400fc5d71fefe3cb4c748da8"}, {"id": "f857fe5f-82ef-3df4-9a61-d7d6b4e578c4", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.51"}, {"id": "f8b221ab-d4cc-3913-9436-2ef22aa8c797", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.5"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "418766be-d639-347a-b9d5-81d380122984", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}], "isExploited": false}